## Development

The default feature set contains runtime configuration support but excludes source scaffolding:

```shell
cargo check --locked
cargo test --locked
```

Enable the development-only `new` command:

```shell
cargo dev new admin/user-add
```

Equivalent command:

```shell
cargo run --features dev-tools,config -- new admin/user-add
```

Build the minimal binary without configuration management:

```shell
cargo build --locked --no-default-features
```

Build the same feature set used by official releases:

```shell
cargo build \
  --release \
  --locked \
  --no-default-features \
  --features config
```

Run all quality checks:

```shell
make check-all
```

## Configuration

Configuration sources are merged in increasing priority:

1. Built-in defaults.
2. User configuration at `~/.config/{{ project-name }}/config.toml`.
3. Project configuration at `.config/{{ project-name }}/config.toml`.

```shell
{{ project-name }} config generate
{{ project-name }} config generate --local
{{ project-name }} config list --exists
{{ project-name }} config show --format json
```

Projects can define a typed application model and load it with `conf::load::<AppConfig>()`.

## Release

Releases are created from `vX.Y.Z` tags. Before publishing, configure the
`HOMEBREW_GITHUB_API_TOKEN` repository secret with write access to `{{ homebrew_tap }}`.

The release workflow publishes binaries for Windows, macOS, and Linux, then updates the
`{{ homebrew_formula }}` formula in `{{ homebrew_tap }}`.

